message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Host-Infection × Residual-Burden Coupling as a Delayed-Risk Constraint Graph"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Can infection, marrow-suppression-like host stress, and residual-burden
  relapse risk be represented as a qualitative delayed-risk graph with
  explicit non-parameters, such that host-context constraints change
  hypothesis rank without becoming PK/PD coefficients or care pathways?
  Four simple temporal networks are ranked on declared windows. With
  burden evidence only, the order is H0, H1, H3, H2. With infection and
  marrow-stress-like windows attached outside Theta, the order is H2, H1,
  H0, H3. A volume-only sort still leaves H0 first. A map from evidence
  midpoints onto k_inf, k_host, CL and ke is refused, and the SHA-256
  digest of Theta is unchanged. Seed 20260921. Not a medical device.
keywords:
  - delayed-risk graph
  - temporal constraint network
  - waiting time
  - competing risks
  - non-parameters
  - hypothesis rank
  - residual burden
  - host infection
  - computational oncology
  - research-only
